{"type": "text", "sessionID": "ses_fixture", "part": {"id": "prt_18016d6b60016a5frs6YujTWbx", "messageID": "msg_18016c6b7001sWP25BJff01NpQ", "type": "text", "text": "**Status: researched and answered \u2014 yes, it can be done, with limits. Build work is running now.**\n\nWhat the research found (verified against the Composio tool catalog):\n\n- **Reddit \u2014 write is possible.** We have real write tools (`REDDIT_POST_REDDIT_COMMENT`), so back-posting to a Reddit source is programmatic. Caveat: replies post as our connected Reddit account, so we confirm the handle first, and replies must be value-first with disclosure \u2014 a naked \"check out our blog\" plug gets the account banned.\n- **Hacker News \u2014 no write tool.** Replies stay a manual copy-paste block.\n- **Stack Exchange \u2014 read-only.** No answer/comment write path.\n- **Named-article authors** (postmortem/blog writers we credit) are reachable by board-approved email or LinkedIn \u2014 the cleanest surface.\n- **Source recording:** the daily run already logs source links per blog; the build extends it to store the source URL and named author per drafted blog.\n\nYou chose **Option C with review-first-two**. Current state:\n\n- Build task [REL-3144 \u2014 Build source-record + back-post pipeline](https://org.baisoln.com/REL/issues/REL-3144) is assigned to the Content Marketer and actively working (started a few minutes ago).\n- The first two back-post drafts come to me for review before the pipeline runs unattended; every go-live still passes the board gate.\n- Nothing has been posted or sent yet.\n\nNext update: when REL-3144 delivers the pipeline, or sooner if the Content Marketer hits a blocker."}}
